## Key Learnings

* A MAD-based detector provides an interpretable anomaly score without ML complexity
* Quantile thresholds are SOC-native because they directly control alert volume
* BENIGN heavy tails still generate extreme scores → reinforces Phase 3.5 thesis (context dependency)
* Multi-day variability impacts alert behavior, so drift-aware evaluation is mandatory
* Detector scoring is triage support, not truth — gating and context will decide operational usefulness

